    "biblicalRoots": "Sacred Scripture and Tradition together ground the celebration of Assumption of the Blessed Virgin Mary. One of six Holy Days of Obligation in the United States. From the earliest centuries, Christians read the Old Testament through the lens of Christ — seeing prophecies fulfilled, types prefigured, and promises completed in the New Covenant. The Church does not invent feasts arbitrarily; she discerns in history and revelation where God has acted decisively for salvation. Eastern Churches celebrate the Dormition (Falling Asleep) of the Theotokos on the same date. When Catholics celebrate Assumption, they join a chorus of believers across centuries who heard the same Word, received the same sacraments, and found in these mysteries a reason to hope, repent, and rejoice.",
